# Practical 03 - Data Binding in Angular

## Aim

To study and implement different types of data binding in Angular.

## Introduction

Data binding is used to connect the data from the TypeScript component with the HTML view.

Angular provides different types of data binding:

1. Interpolation
2. Property Binding
3. Event Binding
4. Two-Way Data Binding


1. app.component.ts

import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  templateUrl: './app.component.html',
  styleUrl: './app.component.css'
})
export class AppComponent {

  name = 'Aarti';
  course = 'Angular';
  college = 'MIT ACSC';

}
2. app.component.html

<h1>String Interpolation</h1>

<p>My Name is {{ name }}</p>

<p>My Course is {{ course }}</p>

<p>My College is {{ college }}</p>

